# preset-1card.args — `vllm serve` flags of the Qwen3.8-27B 1-card preset, 0.32.0-b70.5: one B70, DFlash2 K=7 with the W8A8 int8
# drafter, fp8 KV, 8 slots, 147,456-token context, 32 GiB host-RAM KV tier. One flag and its value per line; pair with preset-1card.env.
# Measured 2026-10-31 on the b70.5 engine and kernels (numbers in meta.md). Run:
# v0.32/engine/serve.sh qwen38-27b preset-1card
--served-model-name qwen38-27b
--host 0.0.0.0
# PARAMETER port: ours is 8000 + the lowest card index; any free port works
--port 8002
--dtype bfloat16
--tensor-parallel-size 1
# 0.97 is the measured ceiling on one card: 0.98 is refused by vLLM's start-up free-memory check (29.45 of 30.3 GiB free);
# 0.97 held a burst and a 139K prefill with nothing spilled to host memory
--gpu-memory-utilization 0.97
--max-model-len 147456
# prefill chunk 4096 tokens (2048 freed only 0.14 GiB on one card for -6 % prefill)
--max-num-batched-tokens 4096
--max-num-seqs 8
# fp8 KV (e4m3, scale 1.0) on the XPU FlashAttention backend: about twice the tokens of bf16 on one card. Do not use
# int8_per_token_head here: on TRITON_ATTN it gave incoherent greedy output on XPU (docs/lessons-learned.md §1)
--kv-cache-dtype fp8
# the text model only (the checkpoint's vision tower is not loaded)
--language-model-only
# FULL graphs for uniform decode: every multiple of 1+K = 8 up to 8 x 8, plus three prefill sizes
--compilation-config {"cudagraph_mode":"FULL_AND_PIECEWISE","cudagraph_capture_sizes":[1,8,16,24,32,40,48,56,64,256,512,1024]}
--cudagraph-metrics
--enable-auto-tool-choice
--tool-call-parser qwen3_coder
--reasoning-parser qwen3
# generic template (relative to the kit root; serve.sh runs there): the checkpoint's own template plus the thinking switch
# (off wins); behaviour and attribution belong to the client or gateway layer
--chat-template v0.32/models/qwen38-27b/chat_template.jinja
# server default temperature 0.7 (top_p 0.95 / top_k 20 from the checkpoint's generation_config); a request's own value wins
--override-generation-config {"temperature": 0.7}
# when the per-effort thinking budget (B70_THINKING_BUDGET) runs out, close thinking with a short transition
--reasoning-config {"reasoning_end_str": "\n\nI have thought enough; time to answer.\n</think>\n\n"}
# CPU KV tier: 32 GiB of pinned host RAM (one 32 GiB block; AllowUnrestrictedSize=1 in the .env)
# PARAMETER KV offload size (GiB, host RAM): 32
--kv-offloading-size 32
--kv-offloading-backend native
# DFlash2 block-diffusion drafter: incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2 @ 015e795, converted to W8A8 int8 (quantize_dflash2_w8a8.py; 1.91 instead
# of 3.58 GiB, so +49K fp8 KV tokens at this util); its GEMMs run on oneDNN int8 (B70_XPU_INT8_ONEDNN=1 in the .env). Drafter attention TRITON_ATTN.
# PARAMETER drafter: the bf16 drafter (/models/qwen3.8-27b/DFlash2, drop B70_XPU_INT8_ONEDNN) fits 100,630 tokens at this util
--speculative-config {"method":"dflash","model":"/models/qwen3.8-27b/DFlash2-w8a8","num_speculative_tokens":7,"draft_tensor_parallel_size":1,"draft_sample_method":"probabilistic","rejection_sample_method":"standard","attention_backend":"TRITON_ATTN"}
--enable-prompt-tokens-details
